description:
GAC Motor, a leading Chinese automotive group, is expanding in Mexico, and we are looking for a PR to join our dynamic team! If you’re passionate about the automotive industry and eager to contribute to a growing global brand, this is your opportunity.




Objective: 

Overall management of the subsidiary new media marketing business. The role serves as the main interface between headquarters and local dealers, receives business instructions from headquarters, coordinates local agencies and dealers, and drives the implementation of content marketing, live-streaming operations, influencer cooperation and digital advertising.




Responsabilities:




1. Headquarters interface and overall coordination

 Receive the new media marketing strategy, business requirements and special assignments from headquarters; develop local execution plans and drive implementation;
 Act as the main communication window between the subsidiary and headquarters, reporting regularly on business progress, results and local market issues;
 Coordinate local new media marketing resources, align agencies and related teams, and ensure headquarters requirements are effectively executed.

 2. Dealer business management

 Work with local dealers to roll out headquarters marketing policies, business standards and special marketing assignments;
 Track dealer performance in content operations, live streaming, influencer cooperation and digital advertising, and resolve practical issues;
 Organise dealer marketing training and business communication sessions to strengthen dealers digital marketing capability;
 Monitor dealer lead generation and lead handling, and connect marketing activity with retail conversion.

 3. New media marketing project management

 Oversee project execution across the four local business pillars;
 Manage local marketing agencies and service providers, supervising project schedule, service quality and deliverables;
 Track data on social media operations, content production, live-streaming execution, influencer cooperation and advertising placement, and conduct regular performance reviews;
 Align marketing resources and optimise projects in line with headquarters requirements and local business needs.

 4. Budget and expense settlement management

 Plan the regional new media marketing budget, track utilisation and consolidate execution status;
 Verify the actual execution, deliverables and supporting documents of agency and dealer marketing projects;
 Handle project acceptance, expense settlement and document archiving, ensuring marketing expenses are genuine, reasonable and compliant.




Profile

 Bachelor degree or above; majors in marketing, advertising, media or business administration are preferred;
 3-5 years or more of experience in marketing, digital marketing or marketing project management; experience in the automotive industry, dealer management or overseas markets is preferred;
 Understanding of localised playbooks on mainstream overseas platforms such as Meta, Google, TikTok and YouTube, and of the fundamentals of content marketing, digital advertising and live streaming;
 Strong project coordination and cross-departmental communication skills; able to translate headquarters requirements into local team and dealer execution;
 Experience in vendor management, budget management, project acceptance or expense settlement is preferred;
 Solid data analysis, communication and problem-solving skills;
 Familiar with the full lead flow of digital marketing, from advertising acquisition, lead capture, allocation and first contact through continuous follow-up to store visit, test drive and closing; experience in CRM management, lead-flow mechanism design or dealer DCC operations is preferred
 English as a working language




KPIs

Completion rate of headquarters priority initiatives and special assignments;
 Execution rate and business coverage of dealer marketing tasks;
 Delivery completion rate and service quality of new media marketing projects;
 Volume of qualified digital marketing leads and cost per lead in the region;
 Compliance rate of marketing budget execution and timeliness of project settlement.




Soft Skills: Data Analysis and Management, Influence and Negotiation,

